oan art, as it contains by far the most important and complete collection of artefacts of the Minoan civilization of Crete.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Stierspringer-Elfenbeinstatuette_Knossos_01.jpg/960px-Stierspringer-Elfenbeinstatuette_Knossos_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Heraklion Archaeological Museum"},{"n":"Heraklion Museum of Ancient Greek Technology Kostas Kotsanas","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":35.341411,"lo":25.135589,"d":607,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-15:00; Sa, Su 10:00-17:00","w":"https://kotsanasmuseum.com/crete/","ph":"+30 281 022 0610","wp":"en:Museum of Ancient Greek Technology","ds":"The Museum of Ancient Greek Technology \"Kostas Kotsanas\" is a private museum focused on ancient Greek technology and other cultural achievements of ancient Greece. It has four permanent annexes in Athens, Ancient Olympia, Katakolo and Heraklion and it is famous for its travelling exhibitions, domestically and abroad. In 2019 it has been nominated as “European Museum of the Year” by the European Museum Forum.","ad":"18 Επιμενίδου","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Kotsanas_Museum_Athens.jpg/960px-Kotsanas_Museum_Athens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Museum of Ancient Greek Technology"},{"n":"Venetian Shipyards","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":35.34211,"lo":25.135209,"d":623,"wd":"Q38284977"},{"n":"Hotel Olive Green","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":35.339795,"lo":25.136116,"d":641,"f":["wc"],"wifi":1},{"n":"Venetian Loggia","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":35.339825,"lo":25.134177,"d":792,"wp":"el:Λότζια (Ηράκλειο)","wd":"Q14175781","ds":"Restored Venetian nobleman's meeting place building."},{"n":"Heraklion Youth Hostel","g":"sights","k":"hostel","la":35.341453,"lo":25.13331,"d":806,"ph":"+302810286281","wd":"Q111124780","ad":"5 Vyronos","wifi":1},{"n":"So Young Bed Station","g":"sights","k":"hostel","la":35